World Train Map Atlas: data licences
https://github.com/Flightmussy/trainrouter-atlas

This folder holds the same routes in two forms, under two licences.

1. routes.csv and routes.json: the route facts

   Licence: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)
   https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
   Credit: World Train Map (https://worldtrainmap.com). A link to
   https://worldtrainmap.com, or to the route's page in the url column,
   satisfies it.

   These files carry no geometry. The facts are compiled from operators'
   own figures, timetables, press material and encyclopaedic articles. A
   few distance and top speed figures were measured on OpenStreetMap track
   instead of taken from a published source; they are a small, insubstantial
   extract of the OpenStreetMap database, © OpenStreetMap contributors.

2. routes.geojson: the route lines

   Licence: Open Data Commons Open Database License 1.0 (ODbL 1.0)
   https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/
   Credit: © OpenStreetMap contributors
   https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright

   The lines are derived from OpenStreetMap. Most are drawn node for node
   from OSM route relations (geometry_source "osm_relation", the relation
   ids in osm_relations), some are snapped onto the OSM rail graph by map
   matching (geometry_source "osm_map_matched"), and the rest have no
   record of their origin and are treated as derived all the same. The
   whole file is therefore offered under the ODbL, including the facts
   repeated in its properties, which stay available under CC BY 4.0 in
   routes.csv and routes.json.

   If you publicly use a database derived from routes.geojson, offer that
   database under the ODbL as well. A map or image made from it needs the
   credit "© OpenStreetMap contributors".

The MCP server code in ../mcp is MIT licensed (see ../LICENSE).
